    "body": "Yeah it can. On Windows, if the scope of the OS watch is larger than the observation's scope, then it can buffer overflow for file events outside the observation's scope. But we can't know that, and have to assume that there could have been events in the observation's scope, so we'll have to send an unknown. There could be a similar scenarios on Mac.",
